//All texts are presented AS IS and the provider of this library is not liable for any consequences resulting from using it in any way. Unless specified otherwise, the following texts for each component are public domain.

// The following relay models have a spice model, which is idealized. Please be aware of the fact that the real model 
// might work in similar way as the idealized ones in some circuits, but also will work differently in other circuits.
//For example:
// - These models have an idealized rise and fall time, which means that the switch time between high and low voltage here is only the time step of the simulation. Real components often have a larger switch time. Relays typically a few milliseconds, in some circuits this might be relevant.
// - Many real relays have a mechanical vibration after switching, in the so-called "bounce-time" so that the connection in the switch vibrates too. This vibration is not modeled here.
// - Real relays need a few milliseconds to switch, in the so called "switch-time" before it starts bouncing. This is not modeled here
// -> So for the users: Please be aware that there are the differences between the real components and the idealized model
// -> So for the jurists: this library is presented AS IS. We are not liable of any consequences resulting from it in any way.
// -> So for the helping hands: there is still a lot TODO in this library to make more realistic models:
//      Someone who has a more realistic model which also works reliably in ngspice is very welcome to add it to the library
//      also you may of course contact us.
//    Also this library only contains the relays from A like "American Zettler" to F like "FINDER". Further relays: TODO

<Component>
    <Description>
        Relay
        A bistable (latching) relay or monostable relay,or AC-relay, depending on parameter:
        -If the parameter ampere_off is equal to Pc*ampere_on, with Pc a positive constant, typically between 0.05 and 0.35,
        then it is a monostable relay: The relay is reset at a current lower than the set-on-current, because the iron core 
        of the coil is still magnetized. Therefor a lower current keeps the relay on.
        -If the parameter ampere_off is equal to Nc*ampere_on, with Nc a negative constant, typically between 0 and -1,
        then it is a bistable relay
        
        This model contains fuses to simulate the fact that the coil and the connections of the switches can get destroyed by exceeding the maximal ratings.
        The coil or switch is considered "destroyed" as soon current of ampere_destroy_coil or ampere_destroy_switch is reached, see Spice section below.

    </Description>
    <eeschema_sch>
        L Relay:DIPxx-1Axx-11x //https:standexelectronics.com/wp-content/uploads/datasheet_reed_relay_DIP.pdf  
        ALIAS Relay:DIPxx-1Axx-12x Relay:DIPxx-1Axx-13x Relay:DIPxx-1Cxx-51x Relay:DIPxx-2Axx-21x
        DEFINE [sw1AX200] 200 
        //                           [nr_switches] v    v[switch_type] (A->NO B->NC C->CO)
        //              DIP|      [U_n]        |-|<->|[<---->|| switch model |-|pinout||option|
        IF[value]MATCHESDIP((05)|(12)|(15)|(24))-[1-2][a-cA-C]((72)|(75)|(90))-[0-9]{2}[a-zA-Z]*THENELSE
            <Dialog type="error">You have chosen the component at ([xpos]|[ypos]) to be a relay of the series  [model].
            Please set the value to one of the available ones, in order to specify, which kind of this series 
            you want to select:
            
            DIPnn-qFmm-ppO
            
            where:
            nn is the nominal voltage in two digits: 05 12 15 or 24
            q is the number of switches in one digit: 1 or 2
            F is the contact form in one letter: A B or C (A=normally Open , B=Normally Closed , C=Changeover)
            mm is the switch model in two digits: 72 75 or 90
            pp is the pin out in two digits: 10 11 12 13 19 21 or 51
            O at the end is the option, and is optional. can be A B C L D E F , but is ignored
            
            For example, DIP05-1A72-10 is a valid value. But the value given, [value] is not.
            You can find the datasheet with this part description at [datasheet]
            </Dialog>
        ENDIF
        
        DEFINE [coil_direction] TopNeg_PosBottom //top negative -bottom positive (when not rotated or mirrored)
        DEFINE [U_n] AS_SUBSTRING FROM:3 TO:5 OF:[value]
        DEFINE [nr_switches] AS_SUBSTRING FROM:6 TO:7 OF:[value]
        
        DEFINE [switch_type] AS_SUBSTRING FROM:13 TO:14 OF:[model]
        IF [switch_type]EQUAL_TO A || [switch_type] EQUAL_TO a THEN DEFINE [switch_type] NO ENDIF
        IF [switch_type]EQUAL_TO B || [switch_type] EQUAL_TO b THEN DEFINE [switch_type] NC ENDIF
        IF [switch_type]EQUAL_TO C || [switch_type] EQUAL_TO c THEN DEFINE [switch_type] CO ENDIF
        
        //DEFINE [R_coil] and [U_set] and [U_reset] depending on [U_n]:
        IF[value]MATCHESDIP[0-9]{2}-1[a-bA-B][0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}[a-zA-Z]*THEN 
            IF[U_n] EQUAL_TO 05 THEN 
                IF[value]MATCHESDIP[0-9]{2}-[1-2][aA]75-[0-9]{2}[a-zA-Z]*THEN 
                    DEFINE [R_coil] 200
                ELSE
                    DEFINE [R_coil] 500
                ENDIF
                DEFINE [U_set] 3.5
                DEFINE [U_reset] 0.75
            ELSEIF [U_n] EQUAL_TO 12 THEN 
                DEFINE [R_coil] 1000
                DEFINE [U_set] 8.4
                DEFINE [U_reset] 1.8
            ELSEIF [U_n] EQUAL_TO 15 THEN 
                DEFINE [R_coil] 2000
                DEFINE [U_set] 10.5
                DEFINE [U_reset] 2.2
            ELSEIF [U_n] EQUAL_TO 24 THEN
                DEFINE [R_coil] 2000
                DEFINE [U_set] 16.8
                DEFINE [U_reset] 3.6
            ELSE <Dialog type="error">R_coil and [U_set] and [U_reset] for component [name] [value] not defined</Dialog>//TODO make message more specific!
            ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF 
        ELSEIF[value]MATCHESDIP[0-9]{2}-[1-2][cC][0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}[a-zA-Z]*THEN 
            IF[U_n] EQUAL_TO 05 THEN
                DEFINE [R_coil] 200
                DEFINE [U_set] 3.5
                DEFINE [U_reset] 0.75
            ELSEIF[U_n] EQUAL_TO 12 THEN
                DEFINE [R_coil] 500
                DEFINE [U_set] 8.4
                DEFINE [U_reset] 1.8
            ELSEIF[U_n] EQUAL_TO 15 THEN
                DEFINE [R_coil] 2000
                DEFINE [U_set] 10.5
                DEFINE [U_reset] 2.2
            ELSEIF[U_n] EQUAL_TO 24 THEN
                DEFINE [R_coil] 2000
                DEFINE [U_set] 16.8
                DEFINE [U_reset] 3.6
            ELSE <Dialog type="error">R_coil and [U_set] and [U_reset] for component [name] [value] not defined</Dialog>//TODO make message more specific!
            ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF ENDIF 
        ENDIFENDIF 
    </eeschema_sch>
    <eeschema_sch>
        L Relay:AZ850-x 
        L Relay:AZ850P1-x 
        IF[value]MATCHESAZ850(P1)?-((3)|(5)|(6)|(9)|(12)|(24))THEN
            DEFINE [coil_direction] BottomNeg_PosTop
            DEFINE [switch_type] CO
            DEFINE [nr_switches] 2
            IF[value]CONTAINS P1 THEN
                DEFINE [U_n]            AS_SUBSTRING FROM:8 OF:[value]
                DEFINE [U_reset]        [U_n]*-0.75 //reset needs current in inverse direction. equivalent to [U_set] below
                IF [U_n]HIGHER_THAN 12 THEN
                    DEFINE [U_destroy_coil] [U_n]*2.4 // 57.6V/24V=2.4
                    DEFINE [R_coil] (6.67*[U_n]*[U_n])
                ELSE
                    DEFINE [U_destroy_coil] [U_n]*2.9  //2.9 = 8.7V/3V = 14.5V/5V = 17.4V/6V = 26.1V/9V = 34.8V/12V
                    DEFINE [R_coil] (10*[U_n]*[U_n])
                ENDIF
            ELSE
                DEFINE [U_n] AS_SUBSTRING FROM:6 OF:[value]
                DEFINE [U_reset] [U_n]*0.3 //not specified in datasheet, assumed
                IF [U_n]HIGHER_THAN 12 THEN
                    DEFINE [U_destroy_coil] [U_n]*2 // 48V/24V=2
                    DEFINE [R_coil] (7.14*[U_n]*[U_n])
                ELSE
                    DEFINE [U_destroy_coil] [U_n]*2.5  //2.5 = 7.5V/3V = 12.5V/5V = 15V/6V = 22.5V/9V = 30V/12V
                ENDIF
                
            ENDIF
            DEFINE [U_set] [U_n]*0.75 // 2.3V/3V=0.77 3.8V/5V=6.8V/9V=0.76 4.5V/6V=9V/12V=18V/24V=0.75
        ELSE
            <Dialog type="error">You have chosen the component at ([xpos]|[ypos]) to be a relay of the series  [model].
                Please set the value to one of the available ones, in order to specify, which kind of this series 
                you want to select:
            
                AZ850-x or AZ850P1-x
            
                where:
                AZ850- are the single side stable relays,
                AZ850P1- are the bistable (latching ) relays, and
                x is the nominal VDC voltage, one of the values: 3 5 6 9 12 24
            
                For example, AZ850-5 or AZ850P1-24 are valid values. But the value given, [value] is not.
                You can find the datasheet with this part description at [datasheet].
                
                (If you want to use the relay with two coils, AZ850P2-x, you need to select that component in the schematic editor.)
            </Dialog>
        ENDIF
    </eeschema_sch>
    <eeschema_sch>
        L Relay:FINDER-30.22
		DEFINE [datasheet] www.finder-relais.net/en/finder-relays-series-30.pdf
		DEFINE [conrad_de] finder-30-22-7-024-0000-printrelais-24-v-dc-1-25-a-2-wechsler-1-st-502827.html
        IF[value]MATCHESFINDER-30\.22\.7\.((005)|(006)|(009)|(012)|(024)|(048))[\.0-9]*THEN
            DEFINE [coil_direction] BottomNeg_PosTop //not specified in the datasheet. TODO ask FINDER.
            DEFINE [switch_type] CO
            DEFINE [nr_switches] 2
            DEFINE [I_destroy_switch] 3 // see maximum peak current on page 1 of datasheet
            DEFINE [U_n] AS_SUBSTRING FROM:15 TO:18 OF:[value]
            //Umin=[U_set] U_max=[U_destroy_coil] and R=[R_coil] see Coil specifications on page 3 of datasheet
            IF [U_n] EQUAL_TO 005 THEN
                DEFINE [U_set] 3.7 
                DEFINE [U_destroy_coil] 7.5
                DEFINE [R_coil] 125
            ENDIF
            IF [U_n] EQUAL_TO 006 THEN
                DEFINE [U_set] 4.5
                DEFINE [U_destroy_coil] 9
                DEFINE [R_coil] 180
            ENDIF
            IF [U_n] EQUAL_TO 009 THEN
                DEFINE [U_set] 6.7
                DEFINE [U_destroy_coil] 13.5
                DEFINE [R_coil] 405
            ENDIF
            IF [U_n] EQUAL_TO 012 THEN
                DEFINE [U_set] 8.4
                DEFINE [U_destroy_coil] 18
                DEFINE [R_coil] 720
            ENDIF
            IF [U_n] EQUAL_TO 024 THEN
                DEFINE [U_set] 16.8
                DEFINE [U_destroy_coil] 36
                DEFINE [R_coil] 2880
            ENDIF
            IF [U_n] EQUAL_TO 048 THEN
                DEFINE [U_set] 36
                DEFINE [U_destroy_coil] 72
                DEFINE [R_coil] 10k
            ENDIF
            //Reset voltage is somewhere between holding voltage and drop-out voltage, see page 1 of datasheet.
            DEFINE [U_reset] 0.2*[U_n] 
        ELSE
            <Dialog type="error">You have chosen the component at ([xpos]|[ypos]) to be a relay of the series [model].
                Please set the value to one of the available ones, in order to specify, which kind of this series 
                you want to select:
            
                FINDER-30.22.7.nnn
            
                where:
                FINDER-30.22.7. is the model series, and
                nnn is the nominal voltage in three digits, one of the values 005 006 009 012 024 048
                
                For example, FINDER-30.22.7.012 is a valid value. But the value given, [value] is not.
                You can find the datasheet with this part description at [datasheet].
            </Dialog>
        ENDIF
      </eeschema_sch>   
      <eeschema_sch>
